{number: 110}
{title: Higher Ground}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I'm [C] pressing on the [F] upward [C] way,
New heights I'm gaining [G7] every day;
Still [C] praying as I'm [F] onward [C] bound,
"Lord, plant my feet on [G7] higher [C] ground."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Lord, [C] lift me up and let me [F] stand,
By faith, on [C] Canaan's table-[G7] land,
A [C] higher plane than I have [F] found;
Lord, [C] plant my feet on [G7] higher [C] ground.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [C] heart has no de-[F] sire to [C] stay
Where doubts arise and [G7] fears dismay;
Though [C] some may dwell where [F] these a-[C] bound,
My prayer, my aim, is [G7] higher [C] ground.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [C] want to live a-[F] bove the [C] world,
Though Satan's darts at [G7] me are hurled;
For [C] faith has caught the [F] joyful [C] sound,
The song of saints on [G7] higher [C] ground.
{end_of_verse}
